# Tests of the `kernel` module; generated from tools/kernel.dsl by tools/build.py. They run under
# `refined test`, where machine and system targets work in the JIT's own process.

# Tests write in the last 4 KiB of machine.state (from byte 61440), which the runtime's own state never reaches.
startTest is test
startTest purpose "What a Linux process starts with is kept and read back: argc, argv after it, envp after argv's 0"
startTest verifies stateAt offsetsState
startTest verifies initialStack keepsStart
startTest verifies argumentCount readsArgc
startTest verifies argumentVector readsArgv
startTest verifies environmentVector readsEnvp
startTest typeParameter none
startTest input none
startTest output none
startTest outputOwnedBy none
startTest raises none
startTest effect use machine.memory
startTest uses memoryAccess
startTest memoryHeap false
startTest async false
startTest maxRecursion none
startTest label begin loopKind none
startTest label begin within none
startTest let scratchAt Int64 61440 immutable
startTest let savedAt Int64 61952 immutable
startTest let thirtyTwo Int64 32 immutable
startTest let two Int64 2 immutable
startTest let eight Int64 8 immutable
startTest at begin do findState
startTest at begin do findScratch
startTest at begin do findSame
startTest at begin do sameCheck
startTest at begin do expectSame
startTest at begin do readOldStack
startTest at begin do findSaved
startTest at begin do keepOld
startTest at begin do storeCount
startTest at begin do keepIt
startTest at begin do readCount
startTest at begin do expectCount
startTest at begin do readVector
startTest at begin do findVector
startTest at begin do vectorCheck
startTest at begin do expectVector
startTest at begin do readEnvironment
startTest at begin do findEnvironment
startTest at begin do environmentCheck
startTest at begin do expectEnvironment
startTest at begin do restoreOld
startTest at begin return ok none

